# The file server: one folder, read and written over the network with a key
# (the REST interface). Off unless switched on; the test uses port 80, the
# port the test can reach.
@net
@disk
@forward
$ net dhcp
~ ^address 10\.0\.2\.15/24 \(DHCP\)
# A key the test knows (the OS makes one up otherwise).
$ echo key TestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKey12345 > /system/fileserver
$ fileserver
file server: off ('fileserver on [PORT]' starts it; it would share /share)
@request GET /api/files/
(no answer)
$ fileserver folder /
~ fileserver: not the whole disk
$ fileserver folder /system/log
~ fileserver: not /system
$ fileserver folder /nowhere
fileserver: /nowhere: no such folder
$ fileserver on 80
file server on, port 80 (saved): it shares /share
key: TestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKey12345
~ the link is not encrypted
$ threads
~ fileserver +waiting
# Without the key, or with a wrong one: nothing.
@request GET /api/files/
HTTP/1.1 401 Unauthorized
WWW-Authenticate: Bearer
{"error":"send the key: Authorization: Bearer KEY"}
@request raw GET /api/files/ HTTP/1.1\r\nAuthorization: Bearer TestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKey12345x\r\n\r\n
HTTP/1.1 401 Unauthorized
@request raw PUT /api/files/x.txt HTTP/1.1\r\nContent-Length: 2\r\n\r\nhi
HTTP/1.1 401 Unauthorized
$ ls /share
!~ x\.txt
# With it: an empty folder, then files and folders in it.
@request raw GET /api/files/ HTTP/1.1\r\nAuthorization: Bearer TestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKey12345\r\n\r\n
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Content-Type: application/json
{"path":"/","entries":[]}
@request raw PUT /api/files/hello.txt HTTP/1.1\r\nAuthorization: Bearer TestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKey12345\r\nContent-Length: 12\r\n\r\nhello, bees\n
HTTP/1.1 201 Created
{"path":"/hello.txt","type":"file","size":12}
$ cat /share/hello.txt
hello, bees
@request raw PUT /api/files/hive/comb/cell%201.txt HTTP/1.1\r\nAuthorization: Bearer TestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKey12345\r\nContent-Length: 5\r\n\r\nhoney
HTTP/1.1 201 Created
{"path":"/hive/comb/cell 1.txt","type":"file","size":5}
@request raw PUT /api/files/hive/empty/ HTTP/1.1\r\nAuthorization: Bearer TestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKey12345\r\n\r\n
HTTP/1.1 201 Created
{"path":"/hive/empty","type":"folder"}
@request raw PUT /api/files/hello.txt HTTP/1.1\r\nAuthorization: Bearer TestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKey12345\r\nContent-Length: 3\r\n\r\nhi\n
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
@request raw GET /api/files/hello.txt HTTP/1.1\r\nAuthorization: Bearer TestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKey12345\r\n\r\n
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Length: 3
hi
@request raw HEAD /api/files/hive/comb/cell%201.txt HTTP/1.1\r\nAuthorization: Bearer TestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKey12345\r\n\r\n
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Content-Length: 5
!~ honey
# A part of a file (what download tools ask for to fetch in pieces or to go on after a break).
@request raw GET /api/files/hive/comb/cell%201.txt HTTP/1.1\r\nAuthorization: Bearer TestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKey12345\r\nRange: bytes=1-3\r\n\r\n
HTTP/1.1 206 Partial Content
Content-Length: 3
Accept-Ranges: bytes
Content-Range: bytes 1-3/5
one
@request raw GET /api/files/hive/comb/cell%201.txt HTTP/1.1\r\nAuthorization: Bearer TestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKey12345\r\nRange: bytes=-2\r\n\r\n
HTTP/1.1 206 Partial Content
Content-Range: bytes 3-4/5
ey
@request raw GET /api/files/hive/comb/cell%201.txt HTTP/1.1\r\nAuthorization: Bearer TestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKey12345\r\nRange: bytes=3-\r\n\r\n
HTTP/1.1 206 Partial Content
Content-Range: bytes 3-4/5
ey
@request raw GET /api/files/hive/comb/cell%201.txt HTTP/1.1\r\nAuthorization: Bearer TestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKey12345\r\nRange: bytes=9-\r\n\r\n
HTTP/1.1 416 Range Not Satisfiable
Content-Range: bytes */5
!~ honey
@request raw GET /api/files/hive/comb/cell%201.txt HTTP/1.1\r\nAuthorization: Bearer TestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKey12345\r\nRange: bytes=0-1,3-4\r\n\r\n
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Content-Length: 5
honey
@request raw GET /api/files/hive HTTP/1.1\r\nAuthorization: Bearer TestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKey12345\r\n\r\n
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
{"path":"/hive","entries":[{"name":"comb","type":"folder","size":0},{"name":"empty","type":"folder","size":0}]}
@request raw GET /api/files/ HTTP/1.1\r\nAuthorization: Bearer TestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKey12345\r\n\r\n
{"path":"/","entries":[{"name":"hello.txt","type":"file","size":3},{"name":"hive","type":"folder","size":0}]}
# For browsers: a page that asks for the key (nothing secret in it), and a
# link for a file, made for the address the browser used, that needs no key.
@request GET /api/ui
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8
~ ^Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'unsafe-inline'; .*connect-src 'self'
~ <title>Files — BeeCodersOs</title>
!~ TestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKey12345
@request raw GET / HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: files.test\r\nAccept: text/html,application/xhtml+xml\r\n\r\n
HTTP/1.1 302 Found
Location: /api/ui
@request raw GET /api/link/hive/comb/cell%201.txt HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: files.test\r\n\r\n
HTTP/1.1 401 Unauthorized
@request raw GET /api/link/hive/comb/cell%201.txt HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: files.test\r\nAuthorization: Bearer TestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKey12345\r\n\r\n
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
~ ^\{"link":"http://files\.test/hive/comb/cell%201\.txt\?X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&.*X-Amz-Expires=3600&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&response-content-disposition=attachment&X-Amz-Signature=[0-9a-f]{64}"\}$
@capture link "link":"http://files\.test(/[^"]+)"
@request raw GET {link} HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: files.test\r\n\r\n
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Content-Length: 5
Content-Disposition: attachment
honey
# The link is for that address: at another one it fetches nothing.
@request raw GET {link} HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: other.test\r\n\r\n
HTTP/1.1 403 Forbidden
!~ honey
@request raw GET /api/link/hello.txt HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: files.test\r\nAuthorization: Bearer TestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKey12345\r\n\r\n
HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request
{"error":"only files in a folder of the shared folder have links"}
@request raw GET /api/link/hive/comb/none.txt HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: files.test\r\nAuthorization: Bearer TestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKey12345\r\n\r\n
HTTP/1.1 404 Not Found
@request raw GET /api/link/hive/comb/cell%201.txt?hours=999 HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: files.test\r\nAuthorization: Bearer TestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKey12345\r\n\r\n
HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request
@request raw GET /api/link/hive/../../secret.txt HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: files.test\r\nAuthorization: Bearer TestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKey12345\r\n\r\n
HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request
# Never outside the shared folder.
$ echo private > /secret.txt
@request raw GET /api/files/../secret.txt HTTP/1.1\r\nAuthorization: Bearer TestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKey12345\r\n\r\n
HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request
!~ private
@request raw GET /api/files/%2e%2e/system/fileserver HTTP/1.1\r\nAuthorization: Bearer TestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKey12345\r\n\r\n
HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request
!~ key
@request raw GET /secret.txt HTTP/1.1\r\nAuthorization: Bearer TestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKey12345\r\n\r\n
HTTP/1.1 403 Forbidden
!~ private
@request raw PUT /api/files/../planted.txt HTTP/1.1\r\nAuthorization: Bearer TestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKey12345\r\nContent-Length: 1\r\n\r\nx
HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request
$ ls /
!~ planted
$ ls /share
!~ \.up-
# What cannot be done says why.
@request raw GET /api/files/none.txt HTTP/1.1\r\nAuthorization: Bearer TestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKey12345\r\n\r\n
HTTP/1.1 404 Not Found
{"error":"no such file or folder"}
@request raw DELETE /api/files/hive HTTP/1.1\r\nAuthorization: Bearer TestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKey12345\r\n\r\n
HTTP/1.1 409 Conflict
@request raw DELETE /api/files/ HTTP/1.1\r\nAuthorization: Bearer TestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKey12345\r\n\r\n
HTTP/1.1 403 Forbidden
@request raw PUT /api/files/hive HTTP/1.1\r\nAuthorization: Bearer TestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKey12345\r\nContent-Length: 1\r\n\r\nx
HTTP/1.1 409 Conflict
@request raw PUT /api/files/big.bin HTTP/1.1\r\nAuthorization: Bearer TestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKey12345\r\nContent-Length: 99999999\r\n\r\n
HTTP/1.1 413 Content Too Large
@request raw PUT /api/files/nolength.txt HTTP/1.1\r\nAuthorization: Bearer TestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKey12345\r\n\r\n
HTTP/1.1 411 Length Required
@request raw POST /api/files/hello.txt HTTP/1.1\r\nAuthorization: Bearer TestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKey12345\r\n\r\n
HTTP/1.1 405 Method Not Allowed
Allow: GET, HEAD, PUT, DELETE
@request raw PUT /api/files/a-name-that-is-much-too-long-for-beefs.txt HTTP/1.1\r\nAuthorization: Bearer TestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKey12345\r\nContent-Length: 1\r\n\r\nx
HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request
@request raw nonsense\r\n\r\n
HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request
# Delete, and see it gone.
@request raw DELETE /api/files/hello.txt HTTP/1.1\r\nAuthorization: Bearer TestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKey12345\r\n\r\n
HTTP/1.1 204 No Content
$ ls /share
!~ hello
$ fileserver
~ file server: on, http://10\.0\.2\.15:80/api/files/ shares /share
~ \d+ requests answered, 6 of them without the right key
# A new key: the old one stops working at once.
$ fileserver key new
~ new key: \w{40}
@request raw GET /api/files/ HTTP/1.1\r\nAuthorization: Bearer TestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKeyTestKey12345\r\n\r\n
HTTP/1.1 401 Unauthorized
# It is still on after a restart, and off stays off.
@reboot
~ \[fileserver\] files on port 80, with a key, not encrypted
@request GET /api/files/
HTTP/1.1 401 Unauthorized
$ fileserver off
file server off (saved)
@request GET /api/files/
(no answer)
